{% decision_card number="ADR-0011" status="draft" %}
One decision. Status reviewed 2026-07-27.
{% /decision_card %}

## Context

A live worker must not contaminate the primary working tree or another work unit.

## Decision drivers

- Isolation
- Recoverability
- Parallel-safety prerequisite

## Options considered

- Primary worktree edits
- Temporary copies
- Broker-managed Git worktrees

## Decision

Proposed: when live execution is authorized, assign one validated worktree per work unit. No worktree executor exists now.

## Positive consequences

- Clear diff and cleanup boundary

## Negative consequences

- Lifecycle and storage complexity

## Risks

- Stale worktrees, overlapping files, destructive cleanup

## Follow-up work

- Threat-model commands
- Build a dry-run lifecycle
- Require explicit cleanup policy

## Supersedes or superseded by

Draft proposal; superseded by: none.

